  "body": [
    {
      "tag": "note",
      "attributes": {},
      "text": "metre: Śārdūlavikrīḍita"
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_1"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "kvedaṃ dāśabalaṃ guṇair aśabalaṃ caryāvibhutvaṃ vibho",
              "segment_number": 1,
              "translated_text": "Where is this Ten-powered One (<s>Daśabala</s>), unblemished in virtues, the magnificence of whose conduct, O Lord—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "janmasyandanikāvivartanajaḍaṃ cetaḥ kva cedaṃ mama",
              "segment_number": 2,
              "translated_text": "and where is this mind of mine, dulled by the turning of the chariot of births?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "yenāvandhyaphalodayās tvayi bhavanty abhyāhitāḥ pāṃsavas",
              "segment_number": 3,
              "translated_text": "Yet by that [intention] through which even [offerings of] dust placed in you yield unfailing fruit,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tena stutyanubandhinā mukharatām ālambate bhāratī",
              "segment_number": 4,
              "translated_text": "by that impulse connected with praise, my speech (<s>Bhāratī</s>) takes to eloquence."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 5,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_2"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "cittālambanalaṅghinaḥ śamadṛśām āveṇikāḥ sadguṇā",
              "segment_number": 6,
              "translated_text": "The unique virtues of the seers of tranquility (<s>śama</s>), which surpass the grasp of the mind,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "vācāṃ gocaratāṃ tu yānti kalayā sthūlā hi vo mādṛśām",
              "segment_number": 7,
              "translated_text": "yet come within the range of speech in their coarser aspect, for people like us;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "ratnāny ambunidher upāmbupulineṣv āvir bhavanty arthinām",
              "segment_number": 8,
              "translated_text": "the gems of the ocean become visible to seekers on the sand-banks near the water's edge—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "antarbhinnataraṅgadyotarucakajyotsnāni gṛhṇāti kaḥ",
              "segment_number": 9,
              "translated_text": "[but] who can grasp those that gleam with the moonlight-lustre of jewels within the broken waves?"
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 10,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_3"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "yā vo bodhipathānuyānamahatām utsāhinī karmaṇām",
              "segment_number": 11,
              "translated_text": "That zealous stream of your great deeds, following the path to <s>Bodhi</s> (enlightenment),"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "āsīl lokahitodaye jina kṛpāviṣyandinī santatiḥ",
              "segment_number": 12,
              "translated_text": "which was overflowing with compassion for the arising of the world's welfare, O <s>Jina</s> (Victorious One),"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "sānekāpacitaḥ punāti bhagavan saṃkīrtyamānādhunā",
              "segment_number": 13,
              "translated_text": "that [stream], now being celebrated, purifies manifold offenses, O <s>Bhagavan</s> (Blessed One)—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "jñeyābhogavisāriṇo gatamalāḥ prāg eva bodhau guṇāḥ",
              "segment_number": 14,
              "translated_text": "[for] the virtues, free from defilement, spreading over the extent of all that is knowable, [existed] already before [your] enlightenment."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 15,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_4"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "uddāmadviradasya rāgavaśino vṛttiṃ puronmādinīm",
              "segment_number": 16,
              "translated_text": "Seeing the formerly maddened behavior of the unrestrained elephant, subject to passion,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "ālokyāvyativartinā praṇihitā bodhau dhiyo yat tvayā",
              "segment_number": 17,
              "translated_text": "you, unswerving [in resolve], directed your thoughts toward <s>Bodhi</s>—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "vinyasyanta ivāmarās tvayi ciraṃ dharmābhiṣekaśriyaṃ",
              "segment_number": 18,
              "translated_text": "as if the immortals were placing upon you for a long time the splendor of consecration (<s>abhiṣeka</s>) in the <s>Dharma</s>,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tenākampitakeśarāntam asṛjan puṣpopahāraṃ divaḥ",
              "segment_number": 19,
              "translated_text": "by that [act], they released from heaven a shower of flowers with trembling filament-tips."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 20,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_5"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "kṣudduḥkhaglapitodarīṃ giridarīrandhrāntarālasthitāṃ",
              "segment_number": 21,
              "translated_text": "Seeing the tigress, her belly shrunken with the pain of hunger, dwelling in a hollow within a mountain cave,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "dṛṣtvā śāvakaghālanaikarabhasāṃ vyāghrīṃ dayāghrātadhīḥ",
              "segment_number": 22,
              "translated_text": "intent solely upon devouring her cubs, your mind was touched by compassion;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "yat tvaṃ valkalinīṃ jaṭājanavatīṃ mūrtiṃ samutsṛṣṭavāṃs",
              "segment_number": 23,
              "translated_text": "[and so] you gave up your body clad in bark garments, wearing matted hair—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "trāṇaṃ tena bhavān bhavādrivivaravyāvartināṃ dehinām",
              "segment_number": 24,
              "translated_text": "by that [act], you became the protector of embodied beings caught in the crevices of the mountain of worldly existence (<s>bhava</s>)."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 25,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_6"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "yat prāleyasitopalādribahalāṃ mātaṅgatāṃ bibhratā",
              "segment_number": 26,
              "translated_text": "While bearing the form of an elephant as massive as a mountain of snow-white rocks,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "kāntārāntaravartināṃ tanubhṛtām ucchittaye vyāpadām",
              "segment_number": 27,
              "translated_text": "for the destruction of the calamities of embodied beings dwelling deep in the wilderness,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "śailendraṃ pṛthulopalaṃ calayatā muktas tvayātmā taṭān",
              "segment_number": 28,
              "translated_text": "you, moving the great mountain-lord of broad boulders, released yourself from its cliffs—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "manye matsariṇāṃ nitāntamalinās tena kṣatā vṛttayaḥ",
              "segment_number": 29,
              "translated_text": "I think by that [act], the deeply impure dispositions of the envious were wounded."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 30,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_7"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "yal lokāmbaracandracandravapuṣā candraprabhatve tvayā",
              "segment_number": 31,
              "translated_text": "When by you, having a moon-like body [resplendent as] the moon of the sky of the world, being <s>Candraprabha</s>,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "kalmāṣāntaśikhaṃ śikhāmaṇirucā dattaṃ dvijāyārthine",
              "segment_number": 32,
              "translated_text": "the head was given to a begging <s>brāhmaṇa</s>—the head whose crest ended in a dark [jewel], with the lustre of a crest-gem—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "nālāl lūnam ivāravindam asinā vyutkṛttamūlaṃ śiras",
              "segment_number": 33,
              "translated_text": "the head, severed at its root by a sword, like a lotus cut from its stalk—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tenaiṣāṃ jagatāṃ gato 'si gurutām usṇīṣavan mūrdhani",
              "segment_number": 34,
              "translated_text": "by that [act], you attained supremacy over these worlds, like an <s>uṣṇīṣa</s> (crown-protuberance) upon the head."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 35,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_8"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "bālān bālasarojakomalatanūn yat putrakān arthine",
              "segment_number": 36,
              "translated_text": "When you, O <s>Jina</s>, gave to a petitioner your children—boys, tender-bodied as young lotuses—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "paryastākṣacalacchikhaṇḍakabhṛto dārāṃs ca bhāvanugān",
              "segment_number": 37,
              "translated_text": "and your wives, who bore trembling peacock-feather crests and moving eyes, devoted in affection,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "prādās tvaṃ jina tena nūnam ahhavan mārāṅganānāṃ mukhaṃ",
              "segment_number": 38,
              "translated_text": "by that [act], surely the faces of <s>Māra</s>'s women became"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "saṃkocāñcitapakṣmalocanadalaṃ lajjālasāmantharam",
              "segment_number": 39,
              "translated_text": "with contracted eyelid-petals and curving lashes, languid and slow with shame."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 40,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_9"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "śayyāsvapnavicāriṇā vanabhuvāṃ bhūtvā purā pakṣiṇā",
              "segment_number": 41,
              "translated_text": "Having been formerly a bird wandering in the forest, resting and sleeping [there],"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "bhinnāśeṣakale jagaty avikale jyāyaḥpathāśaṃsinā",
              "segment_number": 42,
              "translated_text": "heralding the greater path in a world whose entire time-order was disrupted yet [itself remaining] unbroken,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "vistāraṃ gamitaṃ vrataṃ vratabhṛtāṃ yan nātha kāpiñjalaṃ",
              "segment_number": 43,
              "translated_text": "you, O Lord, spread wide the vow of the quail (<s>kāpiñjala</s>) among those who observe vows—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tenājñānarujāṃ kirīṭakiraṇacchāyās padaṃ vo gatāḥ",
              "segment_number": 44,
              "translated_text": "by that [act], those afflicted with the disease of ignorance bowed their crown-rays' shadows at your feet."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 45,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_10"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "yat parṇāmbuphalāśinīṃ śaśatanuṃ tvaṃ nātha bibhrat purā",
              "segment_number": 46,
              "translated_text": "When you, O Lord, formerly bearing the body of a hare, living on leaves, water, and fruits,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "tatkālātithaye kṛpāparicayād ātithyam āvedayan",
              "segment_number": 47,
              "translated_text": "announced hospitality out of habitual compassion to the guest of that time,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "ārūḍhaḥ sphuṭavisphuliṅgam analaṃ tenādhunāpi kṣitāv",
              "segment_number": 48,
              "translated_text": "[and] ascended a fire blazing with sparks—by that [act], even now on earth,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "indor maṇḍalalāñchanaṃ śaśamayaṃ yuṣmadyaśo laksyate",
              "segment_number": 49,
              "translated_text": "your fame is visible as the hare-shaped mark on the disc of the moon."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 50,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_11"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "yat kopāruṇadṛṣṭinā kalabhuvā kṛtvā bhruvor bhaṅginīṃ",
              "segment_number": 51,
              "translated_text": "When the king, with eyes reddened by anger, making a curved"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "lekhām ullasitāsinā vidalitapratyaṅgam āśaṅkinā",
              "segment_number": 52,
              "translated_text": "line of his brows, with a drawn sword, cutting limb by limb, [yet] apprehensive,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "tvām āsīt kṣaṇam apy avikṣatadhiyaṃ tyaktukṣamā na kṣamā",
              "segment_number": 53,
              "translated_text": "was unable even for a moment to make you—whose mind was uninjured—abandon forbearance (<s>kṣamā</s>),"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "manye tena niraṅkuśāḥ smaraśarāḥ puṅkheṣu bhaṅgaṃ gatāḥ",
              "segment_number": 54,
              "translated_text": "I think by that [act], the unbridled arrows of <s>Smara</s> (Love) were broken at their nocks."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 55,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_12"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "yad dveṣī kariṇā cirātatadhanur dantais tvayābhyarcitaḥ",
              "segment_number": 56,
              "translated_text": "When the hateful [hunter], with his bow long drawn, was honored by you with [your own] tusks, being an elephant—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "ṣaḍdantena satā sitonnatabṛhajjīmūtapuñjatviṣā",
              "segment_number": 57,
              "translated_text": "the six-tusked noble one (<s>Ṣaḍdanta</s>), with the lustre of a mass of great white towering clouds—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "kośākarṣaṇavāntabhūrirudhirakṣodāruṇais tena vaḥ",
              "segment_number": 58,
              "translated_text": "by that [act], with those [tusks] terrible with the profuse blood-red fluid gushing from the tearing of the sheath, your"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "pātāle 'pi bhujaṃgamaiḥ ślathaphaṇair adyāpi daṃṣtrārcyate",
              "segment_number": 59,
              "translated_text": "[tusks] are still worshipped even in the nether world (<s>Pātāla</s>) by serpents with lowered hoods."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 60,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_13"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "saṃrambhāt phaṇināṃ phaṇāhaticalād bhīmormimālād apāṃ",
              "segment_number": 61,
              "translated_text": "When from the fury of serpents, from the terrible garland of waves [stirred] by the blow of their hoods,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "patyur yan makaracchaṭāvilulitāt paryastanaukā narāḥ",
              "segment_number": 62,
              "translated_text": "of the lord of waters, [waves] churned by swarms of sea-monsters, men [were] thrown from their boats,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "premṇā kāyamahāplavena bhavatā tīrāntam āpāditās",
              "segment_number": 63,
              "translated_text": "[and] you, with loving devotion, using your great body as a raft, brought them to the shore—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tatkarmātiśayena tena nikhilā lokāḥ kalatrīkrtāḥ",
              "segment_number": 64,
              "translated_text": "by the excellence of that deed, all the worlds were made your own."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 65,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_14"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "śailān maṇḍalino vilaṅghya viṣayāṃs toyāvalīmekhalān",
              "segment_number": 66,
              "translated_text": "Leaping over mountains, circular realms girdled by streams of water,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "yac cintāmaṇinā narendra badaradvīpāntarālodarāt",
              "segment_number": 67,
              "translated_text": "when with a <s>Cintāmaṇi</s> (wish-fulfilling gem), O king, [obtained] from the interior of the island of <s>Badara</s>,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "labdhvā pūrṇaphalās tvayā praṇayinām āśāvabandhāḥ kṛtās",
              "segment_number": 68,
              "translated_text": "having obtained [it], the bonds of hope of your loved ones were fulfilled by you—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tvattas tena samudbhavanti viduṣāṃ saddharmaratnāṅkurāḥ",
              "segment_number": 69,
              "translated_text": "from you, by that [act], sprout forth the shoots of the jewel of the true <s>Dharma</s> for the wise."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 70,
              "translated_text": "//"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_15"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "sāndrābhrāntavitānanīlavapuṣām ojomuṣāṃ rakṣasāṃ",
              "segment_number": 71,
              "translated_text": "Of the <s>Rākṣasas</s>, whose bodies were dark as dense spreading canopies of clouds, who robbed [travelers'] strength,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "khaḍgotkṛttadalair vipāṭitaśirārandhrasravallohitaiḥ",
              "segment_number": 72,
              "translated_text": "with [their] split-open skull-hollows streaming blood, [heads] cut asunder by sword-strokes—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "yan māṃsair akṛthāḥ kṣudhāvyupaśamaṃ svair avyapetoṣmabhir",
              "segment_number": 73,
              "translated_text": "Because you allayed hunger with your own flesh, still warm,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "yogā janmarudho bhavodbhavatṛṣām ucchedinas tena vaḥ",
              "segment_number": 74,
              "translated_text": "therefore your <s>yogas</s> (spiritual practices), rooted in [past] births, destroy the thirst that arises from [repeated] existence."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 75,
              "translated_text": "||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_16"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "śyenottrāsaviśuṣkakampitagalasyotsaṅgasaṃsarpiṇo",
              "segment_number": 76,
              "translated_text": "Of the bird creeping into [his] lap, its throat trembling and parched with terror of the hawk—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "yan niḥsaṅgaratā śivāya śibinā rājñā satā pakṣiṇaḥ",
              "segment_number": 77,
              "translated_text": "because by the good King <s>Śibi</s>, delighting in detachment, for the welfare of that pigeon,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "raktodgārakalaṅkitātulatulām āropitā te tanur",
              "segment_number": 78,
              "translated_text": "your body was placed upon a matchless scale stained with the outpouring of blood—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "māras tena dukūlapakṣmataralaṃ nītas tulālāghavam",
              "segment_number": 79,
              "translated_text": "by that, <s>Māra</s> was brought to the lightness of a scale, fluttering like the fringes of silk cloth."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 80,
              "translated_text": "||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_17"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "lakṣmīm apy avadhūya vāñchitaphalām ākhaṇḍam ādhvaṃsinīṃ",
              "segment_number": 81,
              "translated_text": "Having cast aside even <s>Lakṣmī</s> (Fortune) herself—the desired fruit, complete, imperishable—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "yat tiryakpratisandhibandham adhamaṃ kṛtvā bhavāñ janmanām",
              "segment_number": 82,
              "translated_text": "because you, taking on the lowest bond of animal births in the cycle of rebirth,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "cakre marmabhidāṃ rujāṃ svapiśitaiḥ prābandhakīnāṃ śamaṃ",
              "segment_number": 83,
              "translated_text": "with your own flesh allayed the chronic, vital-point-piercing pains,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tena kleśaviṣacchidāṃ tava dhiyāṃ avyāhatāḥ śaktayaḥ",
              "segment_number": 84,
              "translated_text": "therefore the powers of your wisdoms that cut the poison of the <s>kleśas</s> (afflictions) are unimpeded."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 85,
              "translated_text": "||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_18"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "yat sandoham iva śriyāḥ phalam iva procchrāyi puṇyaujasāṃ",
              "segment_number": 86,
              "translated_text": "Because, [those eyes that were] like the milking-yield of <s>Śrī</s>, like the fruit of the powers of merit, lofty,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "digdhaṃ raktakaṇaiḥ sphuratkuvalayacchāyābhinīlāyitam",
              "segment_number": 87,
              "translated_text": "smeared with drops of blood, turned deep blue with the hue of glistening blue lotuses—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "utpāṭyākṣatalocanadvayam adād viprāya niścakṣuṣe",
              "segment_number": 88,
              "translated_text": "having plucked out both unharmed eyes, you gave them to a sightless <s>brāhmaṇa</s>;"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "tenāndhasya tamasvato 'sya jagatas tuṅgaikadīpo bhavān",
              "segment_number": 89,
              "translated_text": "by that, you became the single lofty lamp of this blind, dark world."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 90,
              "translated_text": "||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_19"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "ity ātmārthanibandhinedam ṛṣivākyālaṃkṛtaṃ darśitaṃ",
              "segment_number": 91,
              "translated_text": "Thus, this [hymn] bound to the purpose of the Self, adorned with the words of the <s>ṛṣis</s> (sages), has been set forth;"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "leśasyāpi na kīrtanaṃ jina kṛtaṃ tvadvarṇarāśer mama",
              "segment_number": 92,
              "translated_text": "O <s>Jina</s>, not even a fraction of the praise of your host of virtues has been accomplished by me—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "tārābdhānavatāṃ jalaṃ jalapurām ākarṣatā vāridher",
              "segment_number": 93,
              "translated_text": "like one drawing water from the ocean, the abode of waters, limitless as the stars,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "velānteṣv iva rodhasāṃ jalalavacchedo hi saṃlakṣyate",
              "segment_number": 94,
              "translated_text": "only a drop-fragment of water is perceived at the edges of the embankments."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 95,
              "translated_text": "||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "lg",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "Js_20"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "a"
              },
              "text": "tvaccaryātiśayāṃśaleśaracanād yaḥ śreyasām udbhavaḥ",
              "segment_number": 96,
              "translated_text": "By the merit that arises from composing even a particle of a fraction of the excellence of your conduct—"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "b"
              },
              "text": "sambhāro vipulaprasādavikasadbhaktyācitāṃśasya me",
              "segment_number": 97,
              "translated_text": "this accumulation for me, whose portion is adorned with devotion blossoming from abundant grace—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "c"
              },
              "text": "tenātyantaparopakāranirataḥ svārthe 'pi mandādaro",
              "segment_number": 98,
              "translated_text": "by that, may people become constantly devoted to benefiting others, indifferent even to their own interest,"
            },
            {
              "tag": "seg",
              "attributes": {
                "type": "pāda",
                "n": "d"
              },
              "text": "bhūyāt sarvavidāṃ parārthaviduṣāṃ yānaikatāno janaḥ",
              "segment_number": 99,
              "translated_text": "single-mindedly intent upon the Vehicle of the omniscient ones who understand the welfare of others."
            },
            {
              "tag": "text",
              "text": "//",
              "segment_number": 100,
              "translated_text": "||"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}